":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@20\"}]}]\na:[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"90\",{\"href\":\"/animal/goldfish/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Goldfish\",\" Name Generator\"]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"113\",{\"href\":\"/animal/turtle/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Turtle\",\" Name Generator\"]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"138\",{\"href\":\"/animal/axolotl/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Axolotl\",\" Name Generator\"]}]\nd:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Fish Names by Type 🐟\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Different fish species inspire different naming styles. For elegant {betta-fish}: <strong>Neptune</strong>, <strong>Poseidon</strong>, <strong>Sapphire</strong>, <strong>Velvet</strong>, <strong>Zephyr</strong>, <strong>Lagoon</strong>. Their flowing fins suggest graceful names: <strong>Aria</strong>, <strong>Ballet</strong>, <strong>Cascade</strong>, <strong>Ripple</strong>.\"}}]\nf:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"For playful {goldfish}: <strong>Bubbles</strong>, <strong>Nemo</strong>, <strong>Sunny</strong>, <strong>Goldie</strong>, <strong>Flash</strong>, <strong>Clementine</strong>. For {guppy} and tetra schools: group names like <strong>The Beatles</strong>, <strong>The Spice Girls</strong>, or gemstone collections — <strong>Ruby</strong>, <strong>Opal</strong>, <strong>Topaz</strong>. For bottom-feeders like <strong>plecos</strong> and <strong>corydoras</strong>: <strong>Hoover</strong>, <strong>Sucker</strong>, <strong>Dyson</strong>.\"}}]\n10:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Turtle & Aquatic Reptile Names 🐢\"]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Turtles and aquatic reptiles have outsized personalities in their shelled bodies. Classic turtle names: <strong>Michelangelo</strong>, <strong>Donatello</strong>, <strong>Leonardo</strong>, <strong>Raphael</strong> (TMNT!), <strong>Squirt</strong>, <strong>Crush</strong>, <strong>Tank</strong>, <strong>Shelly</strong>, <strong>Bowser</strong>, <strong>Koopa</strong>.\"}}]\n12:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"More creative options: <strong>Sheldon</strong> (the Big Bang Theory), <strong>Franklin</strong> (the children's book turtle), <strong>Mock Turtle</strong> (Alice in Wonderland), <strong>Morla</strong> (Neverending Story), <strong>Gamera</strong> (kaiju turtle). Snapping turtles deserve tough names: <strong>Jaws</strong>, <strong>Snappy</strong>, <strong>Chomp</strong>, <strong>Brutus</strong>.\"}}]\n13:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Aquatic Invertebrate Names 🦐\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Shrimp, snails, crabs, and crayfish add delightful variety to aquariums. For shrimp: <strong>Bubba Gump</strong>, <strong>Scampi</strong>, <strong>Prawn</strong>, <strong>Tempura</strong>, <strong>Tiny</strong>. For snails: <strong>Gary</strong> (SpongeBob!), <strong>Turbo</strong>, <strong>Escargot</strong>, <strong>Shelly</strong>, <strong>Zoom</strong>. For crayfish and lobsters: <strong>Pinchy</strong>, <strong>Clamps</strong>, <strong>Red</strong>, <strong>Rock Lobster</strong>.\"}}]\n15:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Themed Aquatic Names 🌊\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Ocean mythology names carry majesty: <strong>Triton</strong>, <strong>Calypso</strong>, <strong>Nereus</strong>, <strong>Thalassa</strong>, <strong>Ondine</strong>, <strong>Njord</strong> (Norse sea god). Geographic waters: <strong>Nile</strong>, <strong>Amazon</strong>, <strong>Danube</strong>, <strong>Caspian</strong>, <strong>Pacific</strong>, <strong>Hudson</strong>. Coral reef vibes: <strong>Reef</strong>, <strong>Atoll</strong>, <strong>Lagoon</strong>, <strong>Tide</strong>, <strong>Mangrove</strong>.\"}}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"Bioluminescent deep-sea names: <strong>Abyss</strong>, <strong>Glimmer</strong>, <strong>Phosphor</strong>, <strong>Lantern</strong>, <strong>Twilight</strong>. Pirate-themed names: <strong>Captain</strong>, <strong>Corsair</strong>, <strong>Blackbeard</strong>, <strong>Calico Jack</strong>, <strong>Buccaneer</strong>. Shipwreck names: <strong>Titanic</strong>, <strong>Lusitania</strong> (for fish that survived!), <strong>Marie Celeste</strong>.\"}}]\n18:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Should I name all my fish in a community tank?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"It's fun to name fish you can distinguish, but in large schools, group names or themed collections work best. Naming a few standout individuals is more practical than naming 20 nearly identical tetras.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"How do I tell my fish apart to give individual names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Look for unique markings, size differences, fin shapes, or behavioral traits. Betta fish and goldfish have distinct enough appearances to name individually. With practice, you will recognize your fish by their habits.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do aquatic pets learn their names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Some fish, especially bettas and goldfish, can learn to associate sounds with feeding. Turtles definitely recognize their caretakers. While they may not respond to a name like a dog, the name serves your bond and helps you tell their story to others.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are good names for pairs of aquatic pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Famous pairs work wonderfully: Bonnie and Clyde, Romeo and Juliet, Lilo and Stitch, Cosmo and Wanda, Yin and Yang. Complementary names: Salt and Pepper, Coral and Reef, Bubbles and Splash.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"betta-fish\",{\"href\":\"/animal/betta-fish/\",\"className\":\"bg-wh